      fix(rust): augment tuple_pattern, use_list, and struct expression for Semgrep
      
      Extend the Rust Semgrep grammar so common Semgrep idioms parse cleanly:
      
      - LANG-479: allow `$.ellipsis` inside `tuple_pattern` (e.g. `let ($X, ...) = e;`)
        and inside `use_list` (e.g. `use foo::{...};`).
      - LANG-495: widen `field_initializer_list` to accept `$.ellipsis` and a bare
        `..` rest marker, so patterns like `Foo { x: 1, ... }` and `Foo { x, .. }`
        parse (base Rust requires `..base`; Semgrep needs the bareword form).
      
      Mirrors the existing in-place augmentation precedent (`field_declaration`,
      `_declaration_statement`). No new conflict entries needed; all 169 corpus
      tests pass, including 5 new ones covering the repros from both tickets.
      
      LANG-487 (standalone-type entry point) is deferred — it requires a new
      `__SEMGREP_TYPE` entry point and OCaml-side plumbing
      (scanner-or-entrypoint), out of scope for an augmentation-only fix.
      
      Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
